{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458823-most-powerful-vampire","id":1458823,"title":"Most powerful vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-05T06:38:34-07:00","id":1458823,"title":"Most powerful vampire","content":"What clan and disciplines/powers etc would you pick to create the strongest combat-oriented vampire? V20 setting. Doesn't have to be physical type vampire like Brujahs,Gangrels and such, sorcerer types like Assamites/Lasombras etc are game as well.<br /> <br /> This is merely a discussion to brainstorm ideas.<br /> <br /> Personally I think that a low generation Lasombra with a high rating of Obtenebration and with Claiming the Dark ritual would be quite broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T06:44:40-07:00","id":1458824,"title":"","content":"caine, what do i win?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T06:49:14-07:00","id":1458825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458823-most-powerful-vampire?p=1458824#post1458824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">caine, what do i win?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, OK obviously excluding Caine, Antedilluvians and the likes. LOL. Those don't count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T07:00:33-07:00","id":1458826,"title":"","content":"I think you measure power different ways among the Ancients.<br /> <br /> Menele can conjure a fucking volcano and wipe out an entire civilization.<br /> <br /> However, he STILL loses to Helena almost every time because men, women, and aliens will do anything for a smile from her. Her power of being the hottest being alive is just impossible to beat.<br /> <br /> Except for Michael is who is the MALE hottest being alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T08:31:04-07:00","id":1458839,"title":"","content":"With such a broad proposition it is a silly question. Anyone with the lowest generation possible and as many dots in Disciplines as possible. As young as possible so to avoid feeding restrictions, Willpower and Humanity 10.<br /> <br /> You must narrow down this somehow for any comparison to even make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T09:34:31-07:00","id":1458841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458823-most-powerful-vampire#post1458823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is merely a discussion to brainstorm ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Adriel/Shaitan/Nergal/Huitzilopochtli</b>... that dude was/is a BEAST<br /> <b>Baba Yaga</b> swiped left Garou septs like theye were nothing, sealed off most of Russia, commanded Koschei the Deathless and the Zmei, and a Demon before Demon the Fallen even came out!<br /> It took an Antediluvian to kill <b>Samiel</b><br /> But the absolute canon killing machine?<br /> <b>Sobek</b>, the Mokol\u00e9 Abomination of the Followers of Set, hands down","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 09-05-2021, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T10:56:32-07:00","id":1458852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458823-most-powerful-vampire?p=1458839#post1458839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With such a broad proposition it is a silly question. Anyone with the lowest generation possible and as many dots in Disciplines as possible. As young as possible so to avoid feeding restrictions, Willpower and Humanity 10.<br /> <br /> You must narrow down this somehow for any comparison to even make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>only 6th generation and above then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T12:01:19-07:00","id":1458858,"title":"","content":"Still broad. Put, lets say, a limit on Discipline dots.<br /> <br /> If there is no limit on choices, so we don't have to give up something to get another thing, except the obvious, it boils down to this:<br /> <br /> Generation and age - the lowest possible will always be the best option, there's no sense in asking. Low gen = more power without any drawback, because before V5 every drawback came from age, not Generation.<br /> <br /> Clans - the only thing that makes them different in potential power is their list of in-clans. If the premise doesn't limit the character in any way about Disciplines, clans make no difference. It makes sense to ask which would be the strongest clan, but the strongest character possible is pretty much clan-agnostic.<br /> <br /> Disciplines - they can be worse or better, but nothing tops having them all. Without some parameter to define this, that's the only reasonable answer: have them all.<br /> <br /> That's why people are discussing already existing NPCs instead of suggesting a build, because framed as it was it is a nonsensical question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T12:12:53-07:00","id":1458860,"title":"","content":"In my experience once you get past a certain base level of power building a jack-of-all-trades character enhances survival chances more than min-maxing up a combat monster does. So I'd say a character with a wide assortment of disciplines and skills rather than being highly specialized is the most generally powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T12:40:53-07:00","id":1458863,"title":"","content":"The most powerful vampire in any game is the annoying comic relief NPC character that the ST thinks is amusing. They have more plot armor than the antedeluvians, they can escape pretty much any situation unscathed, and they have mary sue levels of dot allocations.<br /> <br /> In the rare instance where the PC do manage to kill such a character, they either come back by plot contrivance or a death curse is placed upon the Players so that regardless which character they are playing in which ever game, they will be haunted by echos of that NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T13:22:29-07:00","id":1458866,"title":"","content":"Auspex 6 Clairvoyance and Dominate 8 Far Mastery. With that combination the vampire can control the mind of nearly any being on Earth without leaving the safety of its own haven. No need to fight anyone, your enemies just do your bidding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T13:25:48-07:00","id":1458868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458823-most-powerful-vampire?p=1458841#post1458841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It took an Antediluvian to kill <b>Samiel</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The Antediluvians have killed lots of people. I think what's more impressive is the fact Samiel killed an Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> Granted, he wasn't able to kill an Antediluvian <i>permanently</i>, but it's impressive for what it was.<br /> <br /> I think feats like Samiel's also make for a more interesting setting than &quot;the Antediluvians always win against their lessers.&quot; That's not how it works with elders and ancillae, so I like that we have canon examples of that dynamic still being the case with Antediluvians and methuselahs. Some methuselahs (like Samiel) are probably comparable or superior warriors than Antediluvians, but smart planning and the right powers can render that skill advantage moot. Samiel might have killed Tzimisce, but he still died and Tzimisce was reborn.<br /> <br /> I never liked the idea put forward in The Book of Nod that each Antediluvian is an unstoppable blood god who even an army of methuselahs can't defeat. I mean, to your average vampire off the street, sure, they seem unstoppable, but Revised also gave us three Kue-jin methuselahs going toe to toe with Zapathasura. I liked that, and I liked the Technocracy being able to kill him permanently. One Antediluvian gave the World of Darkness more than enough trouble before he was put down. Gehenna is still scary because twelve (or more!) Antediluvians all rising at once is exponentially harder for the world to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T15:03:58-07:00","id":1459071,"title":"","content":"Absolutely agree. We also have Ravana striking down Dacian, Japeth getting the shit kicked out of him multiple times by far younger and higher generation methuselahs and Troile and/or/alias Set taking down and diablerizing Brujah and/or Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T17:02:31-07:00","id":1459371,"title":"","content":"I would go with Leopold (a.k.a. Gary Pennington) holding the Eye of Hazimel, he decimated the Gangrel while being a neonate.<br /> <br /> Ferox too, because nothing would survive his True Faith 9.<br /> <br /> Monty Coven/Mithras but he perished in V5.<br /> <br /> Antara ibn Shaddad and Tanitbaal-Sahar would be magnificent foes.<br /> <br /> Theo Bell and Beckett are both plot shielded and therefore they always win/escape impossible odds due to their protagonist status.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T23:37:22-07:00","id":1459408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458823-most-powerful-vampire?p=1458826#post1458826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you measure power different ways among the Ancients.<br /> <br /> Menele can conjure a fucking volcano and wipe out an entire civilization.<br /> <br /> However, he STILL loses to Helena almost every time because men, women, and aliens will do anything for a smile from her. Her power of being the hottest being alive is just impossible to beat.<br /> <br /> Except for Michael is who is the MALE hottest being alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a Jojo plotline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T12:25:15-07:00","id":1459459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458823-most-powerful-vampire?p=1459371#post1459371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monty Coven/Mithras but he perished in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure?<br /> I thought his fate is an open door, depending on the chronicle; isn't it more likely than not, t<span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">he ritual is successful and gains his full power and became the ruler of United Kingdom? <br /> Or there is a &quot;canon&quot; ending for him? </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T11:50:21-07:00","id":1459571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458823-most-powerful-vampire?p=1459459#post1459459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure?<br /> I thought his fate is an open door, depending on the chronicle; isn't it more likely than not, t<span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">he ritual is successful and gains his full power and became the ruler of United Kingdom?<br /> Or there is a &quot;canon&quot; ending for him? </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC though the book Fall of London has several possible endings, I believe it was implied that Mithras/Monty will not return to V5 canon. Perhaps we'll see him in V6 when developers and writers change because Marcus Vitel was adamantly mentioned as MET FINAL DEATH in revised edtion and he returned from the dead in V20.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T14:52:17-07:00","id":1459586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458823-most-powerful-vampire?p=1459571#post1459571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps we'll see him in V6 when developers and writers change because Marcus Vitel was adamantly mentioned as MET FINAL DEATH in revised edtion and he returned from the dead in V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if V20 counts for much in this regard. As much as it had some plot developments, since it is metaplot agnostic it is easy to dismiss.<br /> <br /> Not that I totally disagree. I actually prefer to dismiss V5 than V20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T18:22:18-07:00","id":1459604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458823-most-powerful-vampire?p=1459586#post1459586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if V20 counts for much in this regard. As much as it had some plot developments, since it is metaplot agnostic it is easy to dismiss.<br /> <br /> Not that I totally disagree. I actually prefer to dismiss V5 than V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 started &quot;metaplot agnostic&quot; until Beckett Jyhad Diary in which it became full time metaplot and V5 consider this particular book to be a resume and to replace whatever happened in 1st edition, 2nd edition and revised.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T08:53:44-07:00","id":1459660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458823-most-powerful-vampire?p=1458858#post1458858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still broad. Put, lets say, a limit on Discipline dots.<br /> <br /> If there is no limit on choices, so we don't have to give up something to get another thing, except the obvious, it boils down to this:<br /> <br /> Generation and age - the lowest possible will always be the best option, there's no sense in asking. Low gen = more power without any drawback, because before V5 every drawback came from age, not Generation.<br /> <br /> Clans - the only thing that makes them different in potential power is their list of in-clans. If the premise doesn't limit the character in any way about Disciplines, clans make no difference. It makes sense to ask which would be the strongest clan, but the strongest character possible is pretty much clan-agnostic.<br /> <br /> Disciplines - they can be worse or better, but nothing tops having them all. Without some parameter to define this, that's the only reasonable answer: have them all.<br /> <br /> That's why people are discussing already existing NPCs instead of suggesting a build, because <b>framed as it was it is a nonsensical question</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, a hundred times this. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12376\" data-vbnamecard=\"12376\">MowtekPvP</a> you are not really limiting anything, what is the most powerful X? The one with the highest available stats.<br /> <br /> It would be better if you restricted to something such as combat or socially optimized, with limits like &quot;as a starting character&quot; or &quot;with 100 exp points&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On a Vampire vs Werewolf thread, limited to starting characters and close quarters combat, I posted the <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302810#post1302810\">Lasombra Hentai Death-Machine</a></b>. (And if you are curious about the Werewolf side, here is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302784#post1302784\"><b>Ugly McAngry</b></a>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-11-2021, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}